<script lang="ts">
	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'

	const details = [
		{ label: 'Status', value: 'Published', detail: 'Today' },
		{ label: 'Author', value: 'Meeko team' },
		{ label: 'Languages', value: 2, detail: 'es, en' },
	]
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Data and content"
		description="Stat, DescriptionList, Disclosure, Diff, CodeBlock and Prose: figures, details, changes, code and long text."
	>
		<h2 id="stat">UIStat and UIDescriptionList</h2>
		<p>
			A figure with its label, or several label and value pairs. Both are a description list (
			<code>dl</code>
			).
			<code>UIDescriptionList</code>
			stays in one column on mobile.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<div class="docs-grid">
				<UIStat
					label="Views"
					detail="Last 7 days"
					bind:value="1280"
				/>
				<UIStat
					label="Searches"
					bind:value="96"
				/>
				<UIStat
					label="Helpful answers"
					value="92 %"
				/>
			</div>
			<UIDescriptionList
				bind:columns="3"
				bind:items="details"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.stat" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIStat props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. What is measured.' },
				{ name: 'value', type: 'string | number', description: 'Required. The figure.' },
				{ name: 'detail', type: 'string', description: 'A period or a comparison.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIDescriptionList props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'items', type: 'readonly UIDescriptionItem[]', description: 'Required. label, value and detail.' },
				{ name: 'columns', type: '1 | 2 | 3', default: '1', description: 'Columns above the mobile width.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="disclosure">UIDisclosure</h2>
		<p>
			A native
			<code>details</code>
			: it opens with the keyboard and without JavaScript.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIDisclosure summary="Technical details">
				<p>The content is already in the HTML, so the find feature of the browser reaches it.</p>
			</UIDisclosure>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIDisclosure props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'summary', type: 'string', description: 'Required. The text that opens and closes.' },
				{ name: 'open', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Open from the start.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="diff">UIDiff</h2>
		<p>
			It receives a unified diff and marks each line with
			<code>data-kind</code>
			(
			<code>add</code>
			,
			<code>remove</code>
			,
			<code>hunk</code>
			,
			<code>file</code>
			,
			<code>context</code>
			) and a text for screen readers: color is not the only meaning.
		</p>
		<UIDiff
			label="Changes in the guide"
			bind:diff="examples.diffSample"
		/>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.diff" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIDiff props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'diff', type: 'string', description: 'Required. The unified diff.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Name of the region.' },
				{ name: 'emptyText', type: 'string', description: 'What shows without changes.' },
				{ name: 'lineLabels', type: 'Partial<Record<UIDiffLineKind, string>>', description: 'The text that announces each kind of line.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="code-block">UICodeBlock</h2>
		<p>
			Code with its copy button, hidden until hydration because it is the only script. In
			<code>html</code>
			it receives an already highlighted
			<code>pre</code>
			(Shiki with
			<code>--shiki-light</code>
			and
			<code>--shiki-dark</code>
			) and in
			<code>code</code>
			, what is copied.
			<code>mode="log"</code>
			uses
			<code>role="log"</code>
			and wraps the lines.
		</p>
		<UICodeBlock
			label="Terminal"
			code="pnpm add @meekojs/ui"
		/>
		<UICodeBlock
			verdict="good"
			verdictLabel="Good"
			lang="ts"
			code="const count = signal(0)"
		/>
		<UICodeBlock
			verdict="bad"
			verdictLabel="Bad"
			lang="ts"
			code="let count = 0"
		/>
		<UICodeBlock
			mode="log"
			label="Log"
			code="build: 47 modules
build: done in 1.2 s"
		/>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UICodeBlock props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'code / html', type: 'string / TrustedHtml', description: 'What is copied and, if any, its highlighted version.' },
				{ name: 'label / lang', type: 'string', description: 'Name of the block and language.' },
				{ name: 'verdict / verdictLabel', type: 'good | bad / string', description: 'Marks an example as good or bad, with a text.' },
				{ name: 'mode', type: 'code | log', default: 'code', description: 'With log, role=log and no copy button unless copy is set.' },
				{ name: 'copy', type: 'boolean', default: 'true with code', description: 'Shows the copy button.' },
				{ name: 'copyLabel / copyAriaLabel / copiedLabel / copyFailedLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Texts of the button.' },
				{ name: 'uiLang / labelLang', type: 'string', description: 'Language of the interface texts and of the label.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="prose">UIProse</h2>
		<p>
			It dresses rendered Markdown or your own HTML. Text keeps a reading measure, while code and tables may take the whole column. A UI component inside the text keeps its look. All these guides are inside a
			<code>UIProse</code>
			.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIProse as="section">
				<h3>A section title</h3>
				<p>
					A paragraph with
					<a href="#prose">a link</a>
					,
					<strong>emphasis</strong>
					and
					<code>code</code>
					.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>A list</li>
					<li>with two items</li>
				</ul>
			</UIProse>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIProse props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'as', type: 'div | article | section', default: 'div', description: 'Tag of the root.' },
				{ name: 'html', type: 'TrustedHtml', description: 'Trusted, already rendered HTML; without it, the default snippet.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes. The meeko-ui-prose class also works on any element.' },
			]"
		/>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.codeBlock" />
		<p>
			The types
			<code>UIStatProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIDescriptionListProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIDisclosureProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIDiffProps</code>
			,
			<code>UICodeBlockProps</code>
			and
			<code>UIProseProps</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/runtime</code>
			.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
